==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|up-|date}}. First use appears c. 1948. (see [[Citations:update|Citations]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ŭp'dāt|ŭp-dāt'|a=noun}}; {{IPA|en|/ˈʌp.deɪt/}}, {{IPA|en|/ʌpˈdeɪt/}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-update.ogg|a=US}}
* {{enPR|ŭp-dāt'|a=verb}}, {{IPA|en|/ʌpˈdeɪt/}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈʌp.deɪt/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-update (verb).wav|a=Southern England}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-update.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[additional]] [[piece]] of information, an [[addition]] to existing information.
#: {{ux|en|I just made an '''update''' to my blog about my trip to Rome.}}
## An [[advisement]] [[provide|providing]] more [[up-to-date]] [[information]] than [[currently]] [[known]].
##: {{ux|en|He gave me an '''update''' on the situation in New York.}}
# A [[change]] in information, a [[modification]] of [[existing]] or known [[data]].
## A modification of something to a more [[recent]], up-to-date [[version]]; (''in software'') a [[minor]] [[upgrade]].
##: {{ux|en|Our database receives an '''update''' every morning at 3 AM.}}
##: {{ux|en|I have a couple of '''updates''' to install on your laptop.}}
##: {{ux|en|I just made an '''update''' to the Wikipedia article on guerrillas.}}
## {{lb|en|statistics|computing}} An adjustment of [[parameter]]s in a [[model]], or the [[rule]] by which they are adjusted.
##: {{coi|en|stochastic '''update'''}}
# {{lb|en|software}} A version of something which is [[newer]] than other versions.
#: {{ux|en|You should try the '''update''': it rocks.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=John Esposito|title=MW3 Zombies Season 2 Reloaded patch notes: New Schematics, Containment Levels, more|magazine=w:Dexerto|url=https://www.dexerto.com/call-of-duty/mw3-zombies-season-2-reloaded-patch-notes-new-schematics-containment-levels-more-2574180/|date=2024-03-06|passage=The mid-season '''update''' for MW3 is here, introducing quite a bit of content across all three of CoD’s modes.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260901172041/https://www.dexerto.com/call-of-duty/mw3-zombies-season-2-reloaded-patch-notes-new-schematics-containment-levels-more-2574180/|archivedate=1 September 2026}}

====Usage notes====
* In a software context there is a distinction between an {{m|en|update}} and an {{m|en|upgrade}}: ''updates''  usually include important security {{l|en|patch|patches|id=Q208218}} or bug fixes; an ''upgrade'' implies substantial new features and often has to be bought separately (in case of commercial software).

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|modification}} {{l|en|modernization}}; {{l|en|aggiornamento}}

